From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Watermelon OS <build@watermelon-wine-1a>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qt: clamp adopted Vulkan apiVersion so Qt never renders in software

A native backend may report apiVersion 0 when it cannot determine the Vulkan API
version of the adopted device. Qt rejects a zero VkApplicationInfo::apiVersion and
silently falls back to software rendering (llvmpipe) even though the hardware
supports Vulkan 1.3. Clamp a zero apiVersion to the lowest version the adoption
path is built against (VK_API_VERSION_1_1) before Qt adopts the native instance.

This fix is intentionally generic: it does not reference any vendor, driver or SoC,
so it applies to every OpenNOW target, not just the STM32MP2-based board.

---
diff --git a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/LinuxVulkanGraphics.cpp b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/LinuxVulkanGraphics.cpp
index 69d162e9..f3d5fa85 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/LinuxVulkanGraphics.cpp
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/LinuxVulkanGraphics.cpp
@@ -61,6 +61,12 @@ bool Device::initialize()
     m_info.version = OPENNOW_STREAMER_VULKAN_DEVICE_INFO_VERSION;
     m_info.struct_size = sizeof(m_info);
     const auto infoStatus = m_api.info(m_device, &m_info);
+    // A native backend may report apiVersion 0 when it cannot determine the
+    // Vulkan API version. Qt rejects a zero VkApplicationInfo::apiVersion and
+    // silently falls back to software rendering, so clamp to the lowest version
+    // this adoption path can work with before validating or adopting.
+    if (infoStatus == OPENNOW_STREAMER_OK && m_info.api_version < VK_API_VERSION_1_1)
+        m_info.api_version = VK_API_VERSION_1_1;
     if (infoStatus != OPENNOW_STREAMER_OK || !validInfo(m_info)) {
         m_lastError = QStringLiteral("The native Vulkan device returned incompatible device information (status %1).")
                           .arg(int(infoStatus));
